.TH NINY 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
niny \- Niny text editor for the Selviana Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B niny
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fB+\fILINE\fR] [\fIFILE\fR[\fB:\fILINE\fR[\fB:\fICOLUMN\fR]]|\fIURI\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B niny
is the text editor of SDE, written for SDE with SDE-FLTK and cairo by the
Selviana DE Project. It looks like a simple notepad: a row of tabs, a menu
bar (File, Edit, View, Search, Document, Tools and Help), a roomy editing
area and a status bar with the line
and column, the number of characters (and of selected characters), the
file type, the zoom level, the line ending and the encoding. It opens each
file in a tab, highlights the syntax of C,
C++, Python, shell, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON, HTML, XML, CSS, Markdown,
INI/configuration files, Rust, Go, Makefiles, YAML and diffs, and stays
responsive with files of tens of megabytes.
.PP
A tab's \(mu closes it (asking first when it has unsaved changes). The
only tab stays open: its \(mu is inactive and Ctrl+W, the middle mouse
button and Close Tab leave it; closing the window (File \(-> Quit) ends
Niny. View \(-> Menu Bar hides the menu bar; Alt or F10 shows it again,
and so does the Niny mark at the start of the tabs.
.PP
Files given on the command line open in the running Niny window of the
display; a file that does not exist yet is created when it is first saved.
Local
.B file://
URIs are accepted.
.PP
Character encodings (UTF-8, UTF-8 with BOM, UTF-16, ISO-8859-1 and
Windows-1252) and line endings (LF, CRLF, CR) are detected when a file is
opened and kept when it is saved; both can be changed in the Document menu
and the status bar.
.PP
In Markdown documents the row under the tabs offers heading levels, lists,
bold, italic, links, clear formatting and a formatted (rendered, read-only)
view. Right-clicking the text shows Cut, Copy, Paste, Select all and Delete
buttons, Undo, Search the web, text tools (case changes, sorting, trimming,
date and time), spelling suggestions (when
.BR hunspell (1)
or
.BR aspell (1)
and a dictionary are installed) and "Display and Unicode" (whitespace
characters, word wrap and Unicode control characters).
.PP
View \(-> Font\&... chooses the font and its size with a preview. The gear
(Edit \(-> Preferences) opens the Preferences page: theme, font, word
wrap, menu bar, status bar, whether files from other programs open in a new
tab or a new window, spell checking, recent files and the editing options.
Help \(-> Keyboard Shortcuts lists every key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI + LINE
Put the cursor on \fILINE\fR of the next file.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-window
Open a separate window instead of handing the files to the running one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Command palette (every command); \fBCtrl+P\fR quickly opens files and
\fBCtrl+G\fR goes to a line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Ctrl+H, F3, Shift+F3
Find, find and replace (with case, whole word and regular expression
options), next and previous match.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N, Ctrl+Shift+N, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Shift+T, Ctrl+Q
New tab, new window, open, save, save as, close the tab (not the only
one), reopen the last closed tab and quit.
.TP
.B F10, Alt+F, Alt+E, Alt+V, Alt+S, Alt+D, Alt+T, Alt+H
Open the File menu, or the File, Edit, View, Search, Document, Tools and
Help menus; Left and Right move between the menus. Alt alone lets the
menu titles take the keyboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Comma, F1, Shift+F10
Preferences, the keyboard shortcuts and the context menu.
.TP
.B F5, Ctrl+E
Insert the date and time; search the web for the selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B, Ctrl+I, Ctrl+K, Ctrl+1 ... Ctrl+6, Ctrl+Shift+M
Markdown: bold, italic, link, heading levels and the formatted view.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+Y
Undo and redo.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D, Ctrl+Shift+K, Alt+Up, Alt+Down, Ctrl+/
Duplicate, delete or move lines; toggle comments.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus, Ctrl+0, Alt+Z, F9
Zoom, word wrap and the side panel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/niny.conf
Settings (also changed on Niny's Preferences page).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/niny/
Session, recent files and backups of unsaved changes, used to restore
documents after a crash or when quitting with unsaved changes.
